#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054418 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee8b693-8158-55a9-adcd-0ece37ad7226" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations Without the Reciprocal"}] :question/id #uuid "2d0477ef-8561-5404-b97a-99a49031c4ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-13031" :question/problem "Solve for $x,$ if $-\\dfrac{3}{4}x = 12.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides by $\\color{blue}4$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}x & =12 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}x) & =4\\cdot 12 \\\\ \\cancel{4}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{\\cancel{4}}x) & =48 \\\\ -3x & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by ${\\color{red}-3}$ to isolate $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =48 \\\\ \\frac{-3x}{-3} & =\\frac{48}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-3}x}{\\cancel{-3}} & =-16 \\\\ x & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054419 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054793 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08568384-d6f2-503a-98f7-fa3f5052caa1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/id #uuid "9acb3bf7-12c7-51db-a8a6-30111c3b7e86" :question/math-academy-id "e-13032" :question/problem "If $-\\dfrac{3}{2}t = 24$, then what is the value of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of $-\\dfrac{3}{2},$ which is \n\n$$\n\\left( -\\dfrac{3}{2} \\right)^{-1} = -\\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}t & =24 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2}t) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 24 \\\\ 1t & =-\\frac{2}{\\cancel{3}}\\cdot \\cancel{3}\\cdot 8 \\\\ t & =-16.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054420 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfc82dc4-a6bc-5677-ac4a-c1cddf29ab58" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/id #uuid "64b6a66a-c061-52e2-a3aa-e54b7542715c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13033" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{3x}{4}-5 = -8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the fractional term $\\dfrac{3x}{4}$ by adding $5$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n    \t\t\\dfrac{3x}{4}-5 &=-8\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{3x}{4}-5+5 &=-8+5\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{3x}{4}+0 &=-3 \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{3x}{4} &=-3\n\t}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $\\dfrac{3}{4},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal $\\left( \\dfrac{3}{4} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{4}{3}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{3}{4}x &=-3 \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{4}{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{4}x &= \\dfrac{4}{3} \\cdot (-3) \\[5pt]\n1 x &= - \\dfrac{4}{\\cancel{3} } \\cdot \\cancel{3} \\[5pt]\nx &= -4.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054793 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08568384-d6f2-503a-98f7-fa3f5052caa1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "565f57b3-8874-52ff-a3ad-f46714b9f67b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "565f57b3-8874-52ff-a3ad-f46714b9f67b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485917} :answer-field/id #uuid "67f3d8f9-81a1-57db-9f4d-2f2b95d182be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6e3b634-566f-56c2-bc1b-da66c14e5347" :question/math-academy-id "q-179405" :question/problem "If $-4=-\\frac{2a}{5}$, then $a=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2a}{5}=-4\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of $-\\frac{2}{5},$ which is \n\n$$\n{(-\\frac{2}{5})}^{-1}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2a}{5} & =-4 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{2a}{5}) & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ 1a & =\\frac{20}{2} \\\\ a & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054793 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08568384-d6f2-503a-98f7-fa3f5052caa1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6719d7d9-99cb-5eba-80d5-cdccc0af909f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6719d7d9-99cb-5eba-80d5-cdccc0af909f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485940} :answer-field/id #uuid "b72bd720-02dc-5b4e-8d1f-c0c063b0e50c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "030328b3-eb9d-5d4c-9c54-7363627f5975" :question/math-academy-id "q-180220" :question/problem "If $\\frac{4x}{7}=\\frac{2}{3}$, then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we express the fraction as a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}x=\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nWe multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of $\\frac{4}{7},$ which is \n\n$$\n{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{-1}=\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$\n\nThis gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{7}x & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{7}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{7}x & =\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1x & =\\frac{14}{12} \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfc82dc4-a6bc-5677-ac4a-c1cddf29ab58" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77fe170f-009c-5992-b425-2aa44efde624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77fe170f-009c-5992-b425-2aa44efde624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485975} :answer-field/id #uuid "0beb6137-b250-5534-9c90-65c006c787d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "999c5b7d-a89c-55d9-95fb-b94209136803" :question/math-academy-id "q-180262" :question/problem "If $-\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{5}{2}=4$, then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the fractional term $-\\frac{2x}{3}$ by subtracting $\\frac{5}{2}$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{5}{2} & =4 \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{8}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{8-5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $-\\frac{2}{3},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal ${(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{-1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{2x}{3}) & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1x & =-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfc82dc4-a6bc-5677-ac4a-c1cddf29ab58" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40bddad8-62d0-5cee-ba19-2ef46c456639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40bddad8-62d0-5cee-ba19-2ef46c456639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485887} :answer-field/id #uuid "1559fdbb-8e11-5672-be2f-d899f6349024" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83b54fce-efcc-5e43-926c-582ffd8c68bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-180265" :question/problem "If $-\\frac{8x}{5}+3=5$, then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the fractional term $-\\frac{8x}{5}$ by subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8x}{5}+3 & =5 \\\\ -\\frac{8x}{5}+3-3 & =5-3 \\\\ -\\frac{8x}{5} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $-\\frac{8}{5},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal ${(-\\frac{8}{5})}^{-1}=-\\frac{5}{8}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{8x}{5}) & =-\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1x & =-\\frac{10}{8} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee8b693-8158-55a9-adcd-0ece37ad7226" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations Without the Reciprocal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e18e75-099e-55c2-a39c-eeb32cfe4cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053770} {:answer/id #uuid "371b609d-3d63-5502-b962-177fef5436e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053771} {:answer/id #uuid "4f609d16-a553-51f4-b5da-88afeb95a30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053772} {:answer/id #uuid "51123f87-4c88-57ed-91e2-cb5701fbc342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053773} {:answer/id #uuid "6d577407-a819-5ca6-9183-79b25b7e9329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f609d16-a553-51f4-b5da-88afeb95a30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053772} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba46b77-4549-5282-8c55-3bd8c757a1ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "168d74d2-34b0-5fc8-83fe-03641b9c4657" :question/math-academy-id "q-57957" :question/problem "If $\\frac{4}{3}x=8$, then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}x & =8 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}x & =8\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\cancel{3}}x & =8\\cdot 3 \\\\ 4x & =24\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $4$ to isolate $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}4x & =24 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}x}{\\cancel{4}} & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee8b693-8158-55a9-adcd-0ece37ad7226" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations Without the Reciprocal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c52b65-edbc-54be-94cf-212c7038eeb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485933} {:answer/id #uuid "7548c629-bfe0-5d7e-8ac3-1c840d588d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485966} {:answer/id #uuid "838dbebd-5e47-5f14-abf4-1773e0986fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485994} {:answer/id #uuid "86de102e-d41d-5a6a-bf3b-3a656c80ca21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485999} {:answer/id #uuid "a8232765-e2d2-56ed-89d0-082af9d461e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "838dbebd-5e47-5f14-abf4-1773e0986fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485994} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2e4539-eb5a-5c0a-982e-58d125f81f00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f4b957e-d648-5cb2-8f60-5607baf3b66e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75431" :question/problem "If $\\frac{3}{7}x=6$, then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $7$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}x & =6 \\\\ 7\\cdot \\frac{3}{7}x & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\cancel{7}\\cdot \\frac{3}{\\cancel{7}}x & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\ 3x & =42\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $3$ to isolate $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3x & =42 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & =\\frac{42}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}x}{\\cancel{3}} & =\\frac{42}{3} \\\\ x & =14\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
